  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 4 actions (setGPO, setGPOAll, pressKey, setKeyText; src/actions.js) and 4 boolean feedbacks (gpiState, gpoState, memState, keyState; src/feedbacks.js). Definitions are plain object assignments inside if-blocks, no definitions are generated in loops.",
    "Registration is conditional (config in src/config.js): all actions and feedbacks exist only when the model is \"usp3\" (default \"usp3\"; the other choice \"usp_legacy\", DNF Controls USP-8/USP-16, registers no actions and no feedbacks). pressKey, setKeyText and keyState additionally need \"Use as a Satellite Surface\" (use_as_surface, default true) to be false. Each entry carries this in availability.",
    "The module talks to the panel over TCP (TCPHelper to host_usp; port_usp defaults to 50001 in src/usp.js when unset) with short text commands: GPO_<nn>:<0|1> (GPO_00 for all outputs), KYP_<nn>:1 for a key press and TXT_<nn>:<font>_<text> for key text.",
    "The GPI, GPO, MEM and KEY dropdowns are closed lists of 16 entries with zero-padded string ids \"01\" to \"16\" (src/constants.js GPI_LIST, GPO_LIST, MEM_LIST, KEY_LIST); the state dropdowns use the strings \"1\" and \"0\". The module defaults for the list dropdowns are the first entry (\"01\").",
    "setKeyText: the text is passed through variable parsing; the callback replaces the literal two-character sequence \\n with a space and every underscore with a space, because both interfere with the protocol, and sends a single space for empty text. The font size is the config value font_size (\"auto\", \"0\", \"1\", \"2\"; default \"auto\"): with auto the size is 2 for fewer than 4 characters, 1 for fewer than 8, otherwise 0. The text field has no useVariables flag in the definition although the callback resolves variables.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ^1.14.0: options do not support expressions."
  ]
}
